-## 2026-08-29
-
-### 1907 — Partial restart-status cohorts fail closed
-- ROOT CAUSE: The decoder validated lifecycle fields independently, so omission from a recognizable current response could be laundered into legacy absence and reach `Healthy`. `pkg/localruntime/decode.go`.
-- FIX: One cohort gate now accepts only zero lifecycle fields, the complete four-field pre-deadline fixture, or the complete six-field current fixture; `manual_quarantine` is type-checked and mirrored for wire integrity.
-- TEST: Removing each lifecycle field independently now yields `Unknown` with read-failure evidence through `CLIStatusReader` and production `vendorplugin.CheckAvailability`. `pkg/vendorplugin/vendors/local-models/availability_test.go`.
-
-### 1834 — Restart status absence remains distinct from explicit null
-- DECISION: A legacy status response missing `restart_not_before` maps to checked `Unknown`; only a present future deadline maps to `Limited`, while present `null` or an elapsed deadline continues through attested broker facts. `pkg/vendorplugin/vendors/local-models/availability.go`.
-- TEST: Case 27b drives pre/post fixtures through `localruntime.CLIStatusReader` and production `vendorplugin.CheckAvailability`; disabling the presence gate makes the named legacy-fixture test fail by returning false `Healthy`.
-- FINDING: `restart_count` and `half_open` remain historical lifecycle evidence and never mint an active backoff verdict.
-
-### 1834 — JSON null bypasses scalar type checks unless rejected explicitly
-- ROOT CAUSE: Go `encoding/json` accepts JSON `null` into non-pointer `int` and `bool` destinations without error, leaving zero values; `Unmarshal` alone therefore does not enforce the restart-extension presence/type matrix.
-- FIX: Present `null` now refuses for `restart_count` and `half_open`; nullable timestamp fields retain `null` as their defined no-deadline/no-observation value. `pkg/localruntime/decode.go`.
-- TEST: Extension wrong-type cases pin null, malformed timestamps, negative counts, and string-encoded scalars as `ErrDecodeFailure`. `pkg/localruntime/decode_test.go`.
-
-### 1744 — Pricing authority refuses IEEE-754 non-finite values
-- ROOT CAUSE: `Pricing.Validate` used ordinary `<`/`>=` comparisons; those admit `NaN`, while infinities could pass the non-negative list-price gate and make exact system-only redeclaration unstable.
-- FIX: The canonical validator now refuses `NaN`, `+Inf`, and `-Inf` for list and promotional prices before ordering checks. `pkg/vendorplugin/vendor.go`.
-- TEST: Both vendor registration and declaration-owned system-only storage paths reject non-finite pricing; finite cloned authority repeats idempotently. `pkg/vendorplugin/{boardfields_test.go,runtime_test.go}`.
-- DECISION: Invalid NaNs are never made semantically equal; validation excludes them before storage or authority comparison.
-
-### 1726 — System-only idempotency includes complete model authority
-- ROOT CAUSE: `DeclareRuntime` treated equal `(ID,System,Vendor)` as idempotent even when a vendor-unresolved declaration changed `Models`; the losing caller received `nil` although `BuildLaunch` continued using the first declaration-owned launch authority.
-- FIX: System-only redeclarations compare every `Model` field after sorting copied top-level rows by model ID; non-equivalent authority returns `ErrRuntimeConflict` without mutating the winner. `pkg/vendorplugin/{runtime.go,registry.go}`.
-- DECISION: Top-level model row order is presentation-only because identity and rank are explicit; ordering inside a row remains part of its published value. Established-vendor redeclaration semantics remain unchanged.
-- TEST: Field mutations, reordered equivalent rows, and 24 concurrent conflicting effort authorities drive `DeclareRuntime`; exactly one contender succeeds and subsequent `BuildLaunch` admits only the winner's vocabulary. `pkg/vendorplugin/runtime_test.go`.
-
-### 1601 — System-only runtime is a launch binding, not a fabricated vendor
-- ROOT CAUSE: `vendorplugin.BuildLaunch` always called `Registry.ResolveRuntime` and `Vendor.Spawn`; Muse's frozen declaration correctly records an unresolved broker, so the generic consumer migration could launch five frozen runtimes but refused Muse unless it added a forbidden runtime-specific fallback.
-- FIX: `BuildLaunch` now resolves one private generic launch binding: established-vendor declarations retain `Vendor.Spawn` plus fidelity checks; vendor-unresolved declarations with validated declaration-owned models use the same lossless passthrough projection directly into their registered system. `pkg/vendorplugin/{spawn.go,plugin.go,runtime.go}`.
-- TEST: One production-entry matrix drives all six frozen runtimes through `BuildLaunch`; declaration-owned unknown model, missing effort, and forged effort each refuse; typed `RunContext` survives the system-only path; an unresolved declaration with no model rows still returns `ErrRuntimeVendorUnresolved`. `pkg/vendorplugin/{admissionpin_test.go,spawn_test.go,runtime_test.go}`.
-- DECISION: `Registry.ResolveRuntime` remains the strict full-pair API and never returns a `Runtime` with a nil vendor. The broader system-only materialization is private to `BuildLaunch`, generic by declaration shape, and contains no Muse ID branch.
-- STATUS: Component-side coordinated blocker resolved; end-to-end production reachability still requires the exact `TASK-260828-3hultd` consumer candidate.
