-### 1159 — Local-runtime architecture revision 9: registration, status vocabulary, and cancellation were each half-fixed
-- ROOT CAUSE (independent revision-8 review, five findings): (1) `Registry.Register` unconditionally refuses `len(vendor.Models())==0` — revision 8's "register unconditionally, `Models()` returns nil on an absent machine" design cannot survive that call, and would have poisoned registry construction for every unrelated agent type on a machine with no local model configured. (2) Every revision through 8 recovered `Broker.State`'s closed set by grepping `setState` call sites, which surfaced only the broker's LIVE self-report values (`starting`/`serving`/`lingering`/`draining`) and missed three more values (`absent`/`starting-unverified`/`unverified-stale`) the operator-side status function synthesizes when no live connection can be made — so revision 8's Availability table could map an unverified, possibly-stale RECORD straight to `Healthy`, a capability claim with no live evidence behind it. (3) `agentic.LaunchRequest` has no `RuntimeID`-shaped field at all, so `pi`'s `Preflight` could only ever construct a status query from `Model.ID` — one shared `pi` system instance could not distinguish two runtimes sharing a vendor and model. (4) Preflight's own admit/refuse table ADMITTED on its own read failure (subprocess error, timeout, malformed JSON) — the exact bypass the finding named: a failed read is not the same fact as a successful read reporting "nothing running yet." (5) `TASK-260829-188jcf`'s own checklist still embedded the M2 status-consumer obligation as one of its own items, blocked on unscheduled cross-repo work — so the task could never close on M1 alone, contradicting the document's own claim that M1 and M2 are independently schedulable.
-- FIX: registration decision moved out of `Vendor.Models()` (left untouched, still call-stable) into the CALLER (`launchRegistry`): `local-models`/`local-qwen` register/declare CONDITIONALLY, only when `local-models.toml` is present and valid; absent and malformed both skip registration (keeping every unrelated runtime launchable) but are surfaced DIFFERENTLY — malformed gets a loud, distinct diagnostic, absent gets none. A genuinely-empty-but-valid catalog still hits `Register`'s existing `ErrNoModels` refusal, unchanged.
-- FIX: full direct read of `pi_shared_operator_darwin.go` (not a partial grep) recovered the real, closed, eleven-pair `(BrokerState, BrokerSource)` vocabulary. Both the Availability/UX table and Preflight's admit/refuse table now switch on the PAIR, not `State` alone — `Healthy` is reachable only through `BrokerSource=="attested"`, never through an unverified last-known record.
-- FIX: `agentic.LaunchRequest` gains one field, `Runtime string` (opaque, mirroring `Model.ID`'s own type, to avoid an import cycle with `vendorplugin`), set uniformly by `BuildLaunch` for every runtime immediately after `Vendor.Spawn` returns — never by an individual vendor. `StatusQuery` replaces the bare `Status(ctx, ModelID)` signature, carrying `Runtime`/`Model`/`AgentsInfraProject`/`AgentsInfraProfile`, all four sourced from that same resolved `LaunchRequest`.
-- FIX: Preflight's read-failure row reversed from ADMIT to REFUSE. A tenth closed gate (A10) specifies deriving a real, cancellable `context.Context` from `spawn.Config.Abort` BEFORE `BuildCommand` is called, instead of deferring that derivation to "later" as revision 8 did — closes the cancellation half of the same finding.
-- DECISION: created `TASK-260829-1kpj01` (M2 status-consumer widening) as its own schedulable task, moved the obligation off `TASK-260829-188jcf` via a new checklist item voiding the two stale M2 items (the board mutation vocabulary has no checklist-item-delete, so they remain as superseded wording history — the same pattern the review itself already accepted for the `LaunchFactContributor` item), and linked the soak task `TASK-260829-lx3o55` `blocked_by` the new task in addition to `TASK-260829-188jcf`.
-- STATUS: revision 9 published (empty-tree CR, unchanged-tree validation: vet/build/test/regress all exit 0), handed to independent review.
-- SCOPE: `.task-board` outcome resources on `TASK-260829-3jlxed`, plus one new task (`TASK-260829-1kpj01`) and two link/checklist mutations on this module's own board. No production code touched in any of the three repositories. No live local-model process interacted with. `relux-agents-infra`'s and `skill-project-management`'s boards read-only.
